        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Best Practices for Twilite Graph Building\n\nA topic graph of the habits that keep Twilite graphs coherent, composable, and safe to evolve. Each practice is a Claim traced to the contract that supports it and, where useful, explained by the Mechanism behind it.\n\nStart with the Synthesis, then follow a Concept into its Claims and Sources."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "twilite-graph-building-best-practices-summary-view",
      "type": "view",
      "label": "Best Practices for Twilite Graph Building Summary View",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -1967.6044323504902,
        "y": -1121.047422526648
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 240,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "portId": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "twilite-graph-building-best-practices"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## Build outward from the declaration\n\n**Declare identity first, author only what you need, let relationships carry meaning, make authority explicit, and validate the whole path.**"
        }
      }
    },
