          "angle": 345
        },
        {
          "id": "claims",
          "label": "Claims",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 15
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Sparse presentation",
        "definition": "A graph authors only the Views and Content it needs, and Twilite resolves the rest.",
        "documentation": "A Declaration relates to a default View and a landing surface, and may relate to Summary, Icon, and Glyph. One View may serve several roles. Content owns durable material as `content.kind` and `content.value`; a View shows it directly or delegates to a Content node. The authored frame from the Declaration to its landing surface is the graph's shape in a workspace.",
        "examples": "A small note can use one View as its detail, summary, and icon. A richer artifact adds a separate Summary or Icon View only when it shows something different.",
        "notes": "Size the landing-surface frame to include the material that should appear when the graph is unfocused; the active graph's main minimap always covers the whole graph.",
        "definitionKey": "topic-concept",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "topic-concept",
