          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 15
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Cross-graph composition",
        "definition": "Graphs use each other's surfaces through Portals and each other's capabilities through explicitly declared Bridges.",
        "documentation": "A Portal consumes or follows an exposed Port and never creates an ordinary node merely because it was followed. Export Bridges expose structural capability; Import Bridges consume it and must be backed by the corresponding incoming edge. Naming a node type in `dependencies.nodeTypes` describes a dependency but grants no runtime class authority; a Bridge to the class does.",
        "examples": "A collection lists its members with Portals. A graph that instantiates a custom node class keeps a Bridge to that class's artifact.",
        "notes": "Workspace navigation policy (navigate, expand, open alongside) is independent of security classification.",
        "definitionKey": "topic-concept",
