      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Evolving and validating",
        "definition": "Graphs change over time, so edits preserve identity and every change is validated across the whole path from structure to save and reload.",
        "documentation": "Older graphs stay readable, but new work writes the current model. A rewrite preserves `graphId`, `nodeId`, durable address, and semantic type; separates graph extent from presentation geometry; and migrates only rules marked settled. Validation covers JSON, surfaces, bridge refs, class bindings, edge endpoints, handles, and edge-class refs, then save and reload, navigation, and semantic zoom.",
        "examples": "To make a workspace preview fit, enlarge or reshape the authored frame; do not rewrite source node positions.",
        "notes": "View fitting, camera rollover, and edge lanes are still provisional. Do not invent persistent schemas for them.",
        "definitionKey": "topic-concept",
