      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Migrate deliberately: preserve identity and change only settled rules",
        "claim": "Change an existing graph one graph at a time, preserve its identity and address, and migrate only rules the contracts mark settled.",
        "rationale": "Two graphs with the same shape can mean different things, so a rewrite driven by shape alone can change meaning. Provisional contracts can still change, so a rewrite that depends on them may need to be redone.",
        "evidence": "The model inventory's rewrite rule says not to bulk-normalize graphs by shape, to preserve `graphId`, `nodeId`, durable address, and semantic type, to migrate only rules marked settled, to defer render-size and lane rewrites until their contracts are ratified, and not to rewrite source node positions to make a preview fit.",
        "caveats": "The inventory is a working document: settled rules are normative, while provisional items are implementation targets.",
        "documentation": "See the Evolving and validating concept and the How a safe rewrite proceeds mechanism.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "definitionKey": "topic-claim",
